//? Title: Lanczos through actual reorthogonalized stages
//? Subtitle: Original symmetric matrix, explicit Ritz residuals and start-vector limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Approximating a few eigenvalues of a symmetric matrix can be cheaper than
solving the full dense eigenproblem. Lanczos builds a Krylov basis and a small
tridiagonal projection whose eigenvalues are Ritz approximations. We inspect
actual matrix products, recurrence residuals and sequential reorthogonalization
coefficients, retain the original30-by30 matrix and requested step counts, and
evaluate full Ritz-vector residuals. A small residual, a finite step limit and
missing start-vector components impose different limits on any spectral
conclusion.
)

\toc

> The three-term recurrence with full stored reorthogonalization

Start with v0=b/||b||. For each basis vector form

$$ w=A v_j-\alpha_j v_j-\beta_{j-1}v_{j-1},\qquad \alpha_j=v_j^T A v_j. $$
\alttext(The next residual starts from the matrix product minus the current diagonal contribution and previous basis contribution.)

For symmetric A and exact orthogonal arithmetic, earlier basis directions
cancel, yielding a tridiagonal projection. The native implementation
additionally performs one complete sequential Gram pass over all current stored
basis vectors: compute h=q^T w on the current residual, subtract h*q, then
continue. After this pass beta_j=||w|| and, unless stopping, v_next=w/beta_j.
Actual trace coefficients are these sequential h values, not projections
recomputed on an earlier residual.

This implementation stores the full basis and reorthogonalizes against it, so
dense work is O(m*n²+n*m²) with O(n*m) basis storage. It is not a
constant-memory two-vector-only method. One rounded pass does not certify exact
orthogonality. The historical absolute residual threshold1e-12 is retained and
is not scale invariant; at most min(requested,n) basis vectors are formed. Exact
zero and tiny nonzero starts are distinguished using a widened norm fallback
when ordinary squares underflow/overflow.

> Two dimensions: see the actual producing stages

For A=[[2,1],[1,2]] and b=(1,0), the first product is(2,1), alpha2, three-term
residual(0,1) and beta1. The next basis vector is(0,1), after which the residual
is zero. The actual projected eigenvalues are3 and1.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lanczos_stages.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::vector<std::vector<double>> A = {{2, 1}, {1, 2}};
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::lanczos_trace(A, {1, 0}, 2);
    std::print("| actual iteration | alpha | previous beta | residual norm after full Gram pass |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12f} | {:.12e} |\n", e.iteration,
                   e.alpha, e.beta_previous, e.residual_norm);
    std::print("\n| actual iteration | projected basis identity | actual sequential Gram coefficient |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.projections)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {:.12e} |\n", e.iteration, e.basis_index,
                   e.coefficient);
    const auto r = dm::algorithms::lanczos_ritz_analysis(A, t.result);
    std::print("\n| actual Ritz mode | native value | explicit full-matrix residual norm |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.values.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {:.12f} | {:.12e} |\n", i, r.values[i],
                   r.residual_norms[i]);
    const auto &e = t.steps.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("av", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual A times v\n({}, {})", e.matrix_product[0],
                       e.matrix_product[1])).node("three", {6, 0},
                                                  std::format(
                                                  "Actual three-term residual\n({}, {})",
                                                  e.three_term[0],
                                                  e.three_term[1])).node(
        "gram", {12, 0},
        std::format("Actual after full Gram pass\n({}, {})", e.residual[0],
                    e.residual[1])).node("beta", {18, 0},
                                         std::format("Actual residual norm\n{}",
                                                     e.residual_norm)).edge(
        "av", "three").edge("three", "gram").edge("gram", "beta").save_svg(
        "build/lanczos_stages.svg");
}
```
