> Checking actual dense and reorthogonalization work

For d completed iterations, matrix-vector calls equal d and scalar matrix
products equal n²*d. One full Gram pass projects against1,2,…,d stored vectors,
giving d(d+1)/2 actual projections and d+d(d+1)/2 counted alpha/Gram inner
products. Initial plus residual norms give d+1 calls on a nonzero attempted run.
Counts exclude coordinate norm arithmetic, validation, copying, allocation and
time. The basis/storage and reorthogonalization cost must not be hidden by
describing only the three-term recurrence.

Use a finite exactly symmetric64-by64 tridiagonal with diagonal1 through64 and
off-diagonal0.25, and perform each requested complete run separately. The table
checks actual counter identities using actual retained d rather than assuming
every requested step was executed.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/lanczos_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    constexpr std::size_t n = 64;
    std::vector<std::vector<double>> A(n, std::vector<double>(n));
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        A[i][i] = i + 1;
        if (i + 1 < n)
            A[i][i + 1] = A[i + 1][i] = .25;
    }
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    std::print("| actual requested steps | actual retained d | actual matvec calls | actual scalar matrix " "products | n squared times d | actual Gram projections | d times d plus1 over2 | actual " "counted inner products | actual norm calls |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (int m : {4, 8, 16, 32, 48}) {
        const auto t =
            dm::algorithms::lanczos_trace(A, std::vector<double>(n, 1), m);
        const auto d = t.result.alpha.size();
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", m, d,
                   t.work.matvecs, t.work.matrix_products, n * n * d,
                   t.work.reorth_projections, d * (d + 1) / 2,
                   t.work.dot_products, t.work.norm_evaluations);
        x.push_back(d);
        y.push_back(t.work.reorth_projections);
        z.push_back(t.work.matvecs);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "Gram calls", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, y, "", {37, 99, 235},
                                                        4).line(x, z,
                                                                "matvec calls",
                                                                {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Actual full-basis reorthogonalization call counts").x_label("actual retained basis vectors").y_label("actual selected operation calls").save_svg("build/lanczos_work.svg");
}
```
