> Scope and verification

Inputs are completely finite, square, exactly symmetric and matched, with
nonnegative requested steps. The native residual threshold is absolute1e-12;
full dimension bounds the basis even if a tiny residual remains. Historical beta
layout is retained: first d−1 entries form T, with a possible extra actual
terminal residual norm when stopping before the requested count. Ritz analysis
checks complete shape/finite/mode geometry, but does not certify that supplied
coefficients came from the supplied matrix.

Trace capture owns original matrix/start, actual stage vectors and actual
sequential Gram coefficients. The million-entry default counts n*n+n
originals,1+3*n per stage and each Gram record, admitted before its producing
work; zero disables only this optional ceiling. Result basis/coefficients,
runtime copies, fields/capacities and bytes/RAM are excluded. All diagnostics
are rounded observations, not rigorous interval certificates or a universal
convergence rate.

Independent NumPy eigensystems and explicit full-matrix residual calculations
checked13 studies,133 actual stages,1223 actual Gram coefficients and all13 Ritz
analyses, including the original exact LCG matrix. Diagnostics checked actual
basis orthogonality, projection defects, formed vectors and residual proximity
to some eigenvalue, while preserving the missing-component and
absolute-threshold counterexamples. All100 ordinary frozen fits matched alpha,
beta and complete basis bitwise. Native controls include analytic full
tridiagonal spectra, original full basis, tiny/zero starts, complete
shape/symmetry/quota guards and ownership. The ten-report shared build passed141
native CTest cases,45 directly instrumented address/undefined-behaviour
sanitizer cases,90 compiled/executed public examples,412/412 scoped file
definitions plus11/11 changed lagged-Fibonacci engine definitions, and ten
representative clangd hovers. All four complete report programs executed and all
four native figures were visually reviewed. Receipts and repeatable checks are
retained under `build/mepml-conversion/batch-184-193/`.

> References

C. Lanczos(1950),
[An Iteration Method for the Solution of the Eigenvalue Problem of Linear Differential and Integral Operators|https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/jres/045/jresv45n4p255_A1b.pdf],
Journal of Research of the National Bureau of Standards45(4),255–282. One-pass
full reorthogonalization, finite-arithmetic guards, absolute stopping and
explicit full residual diagnostics are the native variant used here.
